# An op-amp amplifying the signal generator's sine eleven times and playing it through a speaker, with
# a push-pull pair to do the lifting.
#
# U1 on its own could not drive the speaker: it gives at most 25 mA, which across 8 Ω is a fifth of a
# volt, and asked for more it flattens the peaks. So its output drives the bases of Q1 and Q2, an NPN
# and a PNP with their emitters together: Q1 pushes current into the speaker on the way up, Q2 pulls
# it out on the way down, and U1 supplies only their base currents, a few hundredths as much.
#
# Between them is a gap: around zero neither transistor conducts until U1's output is a base drop
# above or below the speaker, so on its own the pair would leave a notch at every crossing. RF takes
# the feedback from the speaker, after the pair, so U1 sees the notch and closes it, jumping its output
# across the gap faster than the ear can hear: watch DRIVE leap by about 1.3 V at each crossing while
# OUT stays a clean sine. The gain is 1 + RF / RG, 11, and 50 mV in is 0.55 V out.
#
# The speaker plays while the clock runs at a second a second; `m` mutes it. Click the generator to
# change the tone or the level.

speed 1
start settled

battery   BP    40 0  40 8   12V
battery   BN    40 8  40 16  12V
ground          40 8
wire            12 0  40 0
wire            12 16 40 16

gen       G1    4 9   4 13   sine 440 50m
ground          4 13
wire            4 9   10 9

opamp     U1    12 8  TL072
wire            12 6  12 0
wire            12 10 12 16

# The gain: RG from the inverting input to ground, RF back from the speaker.
wire            10 7  10 2
resistor  RG    10 5  6 5    1k
ground          6 5
wire            10 2  14 2
resistor  RF    14 2  18 2   10k
wire            18 2  26 2
wire            26 2  26 8

# The push-pull pair, its bases on U1's output and its emitters on the speaker.
wire            14 8  18 8
wire            18 6  18 10
npn       Q1    20 3  18 6   20 8   2N3904
pnp       Q2    20 13 18 10  20 8   2N3906
wire            20 3  20 0
wire            20 13 20 16
wire            20 8  26 8
speaker   SPK   24 8  24 12  8
ground          24 12

label     in    7 9
label     out   26 8
meter     IN    4 9   4 13
meter     DRIVE 18 10 24 12
meter     OUT   24 8  24 12
